
# Supabase project credentials. Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the
# values from your Supabase project settings (Project Settings > API).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Not needed yet — no real production domain has been chosen for this
# project (see src/app/robots.ts and src/lib/site-url.ts's doc comments).
# Set this to the real https:// origin once one is, so page metadata
# (src/app/layout.tsx's metadataBase) and email links sent with no request
# Origin header (src/lib/email/notification-triggers.ts) point at it
# instead of the placeholder default.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# Signup confirmation emails are sent by Supabase Auth itself (supabase.auth.signUp
# in src/lib/supabase/auth-actions.ts) — there is no env var here for that, and
# adding one would do nothing. Supabase's own default mailer is shared and rate-
# limited (a few emails/hour) and is meant for local development only; if
# confirmation emails aren't arriving in production, configure a real provider in
# the Supabase Dashboard under Authentication > SMTP Settings (enable "Custom
# SMTP"), and confirm Authentication > URL Configuration lists this app's actual
# Site URL and /auth/callback redirect URLs for every environment. None of that is
# configurable from this repo.

# Required for: the two cron endpoints (src/app/api/cron/*, via
# src/lib/email/notification-events.ts and createServiceRoleClient), the
# admin dashboard's total-user count, and the billing webhook handler
# (src/app/api/billing/webhook/route.ts). Bypasses Row Level Security
# entirely — server-only, never exposed to the client, never prefixed
# NEXT_PUBLIC_. From Project Settings > API > service_role secret.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# PayTabs (see the Phase 3D report for why this provider was chosen: Iraq
# merchant eligibility, confirmed via PayTabs' own Iraq page and its
# partnership with Amwal, a Central Bank of Iraq-licensed processor). All
# three are server-only — never exposed to the client, never prefixed
# NEXT_PUBLIC_. Once all three are set, src/lib/billing/provider-registry.ts
# starts returning a real PayTabs-backed adapter and /upgrade's checkout
# button actually works. Leave any unset to keep the existing honest "not
# connected" behavior (checkout shows "Billing isn't connected yet", the
# webhook route responds 501).
#
# PAYTABS_PROFILE_ID / PAYTABS_SERVER_KEY: from the PayTabs merchant
# dashboard, Developers > Key Management, once a real Iraq-eligible merchant
# account exists and has passed KYC (see the Phase 3D report for the exact
# documents PayTabs requires: trade license/MOA, owner ID or passport, bank
# account statement).
# PAYTABS_PROFILE_ID=
# PAYTABS_SERVER_KEY=

# The exact API domain PayTabs assigns this merchant account (e.g.
# https://secure.paytabs.com, or a region-specific domain) — confirm this
# with PayTabs support/the account manager; do not guess, a wrong domain
# would silently send real payment requests nowhere useful.
# PAYTABS_BASE_URL=

# NOTE: automatic recurring re-billing (PayTabs "Repeat Billing"/Agreements)
# is NOT wired up yet even once the above are set — it requires "Recurring
# mode" to be enabled by a PayTabs account manager first (not self-serve),
# plus several request/response details public PayTabs docs don't specify.
# See src/lib/billing/providers/paytabs.ts's doc comment and the Phase 3D
# report's "Recurring billing activation checklist" for exactly what to
# confirm before that can be implemented. Until then, a successful checkout
# grants one billing period of premium access, same as today.

# Resend API key (server-only, never NEXT_PUBLIC_). Once this and
# EMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS are both set, src/lib/email/provider-registry.ts starts
# returning a real Resend-backed adapter and real emails go out for welcome,
# milestone, and inactive-learner-reminder messages. Leave both unset to keep
# emails logged-only ("queued") instead of actually sent — e.g. in local dev.
# EMAIL_PROVIDER_API_KEY=

# The "from" address Resend sends as — must be on a domain verified in the
# Resend dashboard (Domains > Add Domain, then the DNS records it gives you).
# Either a bare address ("noreply@yourdomain.com") or "Name <address>".
# EMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS=

# Not needed yet — the AI translation pipeline (see the multilingual-
# content-architecture Phase 3 work) has no provider connected until this is
# set. Once it is, src/lib/translation/provider-registry.ts starts returning
# a real Anthropic-backed provider and the admin "Generate translation"
# action becomes usable. Server-only: never exposed to the client, never
# prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Which Claude model the translation pipeline calls
# (src/lib/translation/anthropic-provider.ts) — defaults to Claude Sonnet 5
# if unset.
# TRANSLATION_MODEL=

# Nothing to configure for narration to work at all: with none of the
# variables below set, src/lib/voice/provider-registry.ts automatically uses
# Edge-TTS (Microsoft Edge's built-in Read Aloud neural voices) — free, no
# API key, no account, no signup, works immediately. Set up an Edge-TTS
# voice in Admin > Voice > "Edge-TTS voices" ("Add suggested voices" seeds
# several real voices in one click) and pick a "Default narration voice" in
# the Narration settings card below it. The variables below are entirely
# optional upgrades, tried in this order (ElevenLabs, then Cartesia, then
# Hume AI, then Edge-TTS), each falling back to the next if
# unset/unavailable:

# ElevenLabs — the original (paid) expressive-narration provider. Covers
# Stories, Conversation lessons, and Books. Server-only: never exposed to
# the client, never prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# Cartesia — a paid expressive-narration provider, used only when
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY above is NOT set. Get a key at https://play.cartesia.ai
# (Settings > API Keys). In this app: Admin > Voice > "Cartesia voices" —
# search Cartesia's catalog and add the ones you want (or paste a voice id
# directly), then set the Model field in the Narration settings card to a
# Cartesia model id (e.g. "sonic-2") and pick a default narration voice.
# Server-only: never exposed to the client, never prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# CARTESIA_API_KEY=

# Hume AI — a paid expressive-narration provider, used only when none of the
# providers above are set. Get a key at https://app.hume.ai/keys. In this
# app: Admin > Voice > "Hume AI voices" — browse Hume's Voice Library and add
# the ones you want (or paste a voice id directly), then pick a default
# narration voice in the Narration settings card. Server-only: never exposed
# to the client, never prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# HUME_API_KEY=

# Which Claude model the Voice Director (src/lib/voice/director.ts) calls to
# turn a story's sentences into per-sentence delivery direction — defaults
# to Claude Sonnet 5 (same tier as TRANSLATION_MODEL) if unset.
# VOICE_DIRECTOR_MODEL=

# Required for all four cron endpoints (src/app/api/cron/inactive-learners,
# src/app/api/cron/translation-sweep, src/app/api/cron/voice-sweep, and
# src/app/api/cron/kokoro-voice-sweep) to run at all: a long random value
# shared between the scheduler and this app, checked as
# `Authorization: Bearer <value>` (both GET, for a platform scheduler, and
# POST, for a manual/other caller). Without it, every one of these endpoints
# always responds 501 and never runs. If deploying to Vercel with the
# vercel.json crons in this repo, set this as a Vercel project env var —
# Vercel automatically sends it as that same `Authorization: Bearer` header
# on every cron-triggered request, so no other wiring is needed.
# Generate with e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`.
# CRON_SECRET=

# Cloudflare Turnstile — bot protection on the sign-up form (see
# register-form.tsx and src/lib/turnstile/verify.ts). Free, no card
# required. Leave both unset to keep sign-up exactly as it was before this
# was added (no CAPTCHA shown, no server-side check run).
#
# To get these two values at no cost:
#   1. Go to https://dash.cloudflare.com/?to=/:account/turnstile and sign in
#      (a free Cloudflare account is enough — no domain/DNS setup needed).
#   2. Add a site: any name, add this app's real domain (and "localhost" for
#      local development), widget mode "Managed".
#   3. Copy the Site Key into NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY (safe to expose
#      to the client — it's meant to be public) and the Secret Key into
#      TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY (server-only, never expose this one).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=

# Sentry — production error monitoring (see sentry.client.config.ts,
# sentry.server.config.ts, sentry.edge.config.ts). Free tier: 5,000
# errors/month, no card required. Leave unset to keep today's behavior
# (errors only visible via console.error/server logs, nothing tracked).
#
# To get this at no cost:
#   1. Create a free account at https://sentry.io/signup/.
#   2. Create a project: platform "Next.js".
#   3. Project Settings > Client Keys (DSN) — copy the DSN value below.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=
#
# Optional: lets Sentry upload readable stack traces (source maps) instead
# of minified ones, and needs an auth token from
# https://sentry.io/settings/account/api/auth-tokens/ (scope: project:releases).
# Safe to leave unset — builds still work, error reports are just harder to
# read.
# SENTRY_ORG=
# SENTRY_PROJECT=
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=
